menu "Siri BLE Bridge"

    config SIRI_REMOTE_MAC
        string "Siri Remote BLE MAC address"
        default "e0:c3:ea:9a:7e:d0"
        help
            BLE MAC of the Apple Siri Remote gen-3 to pair with. Gen-3 units
            use static random addresses — each unit has its own MAC, and there
            is no public OUI to filter on.

            To find yours: flash once, put the remote in pairing mode (hold
            Back + Volume Up for 5 seconds), and watch the UART for an
            advertisement at strong RSSI (> -50 dBm). The MAC on that line
            goes here. Lives in sdkconfig (gitignored), so it never enters git.

            Format: lowercase hex, colon-separated, e.g. e0:c3:ea:9a:7e:d0.

endmenu
